./logs/RockyLinux9/messages                                                                                          ┋20221007T221842.000000000┋Oct  8 06:18:42 localhost setroubleshoot[738]: SELinux is preventing /usr/sbin/chronyd from read access on the lnk_file gnutls.config.#012#012*****  Plugin file (35.3 confidence) suggests   ******************************#012#012This is caused by a newly created file system.#012Then you need to add labels to it.#012Do#012/sbin/restorecon -R -v gnutls.config#012#012*****  Plugin file (35.3 confidence) suggests   ******************************#012#012If you think this is caused by a badly mislabeled machine.#012Then you need to fully relabel.#012Do#012touch /.autorelabel; reboot#012#012*****  Plugin catchall_labels (6.31 confidence) suggests   *******************#012#012If you want to allow chronyd to have read access on the gnutls.config lnk_file#012Then you need to change the label on gnutls.config#012Do#012# semanage fcontext -a -t FILE_TYPE 'gnutls.config'#012where FILE_TYPE is one of the following: admin_home_t, bin_t, boot_t, cert_t, cgroup_t, courier_exec_t, device_t, devlog_t, etc_runtime_t, etc_t, exim_exec_t, file_context_t, fonts_cache_t, fonts_t, gpsd_tmpfs_t, ld_so_t, lib_t, locale_t, man_cache_t, man_t, net_conf_t, postfix_postdrop_t, proc_t, root_t, rpm_script_tmp_t, security_t, sendmail_exec_t, shell_exec_t, src_t, sssd_var_lib_t, sysfs_t, system_conf_t, system_db_t, system_dbusd_var_lib_t, systemd_userdbd_runtime_t, textrel_shlib_t, timemaster_tmpfs_t, tmp_t, usr_t, var_run_t, var_t, virt_var_lib_t.#012Then execute:#012restorecon -v 'gnutls.config'#012#012#012*****  Plugin catchall (1.66 confidence) suggests   **************************#012#012If you believe that chronyd should be allowed read access on the gnutls.config lnk_file by default.#012Then you should report this as a bug.#012You can generate a local policy module to allow this access.#012Do#012allow this access for now by executing:#012# ausearch -c 'chronyd' --raw | audit2allow -M my-chronyd#012# semodule -X 300 -i my-chronyd.pp#012
